    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 618, the Tang Dynasty pushed Chinese power deep into Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia">Asia</a> and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#changan">Chang'an</a> one of the world's great cities.</li><li>Its law code, government model and Buddhist culture were adopted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#korea">Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vietnam">Vietnam</a> and shaped East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia">Asia</a> for centuries.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> left power with regional generals; the Huang Chao uprising finished it and a warlord deposed the last emperor in 907.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Diamond Sutra of 868, found at Dunhuang, is the oldest surviving dated printed book in the world.</p></aside>
    </section>

